e": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Iowa enters the 2028 presidential race as an open contest, with the term-limited incumbent leaving both major parties to nominate fresh standard-bearers. The state's partisan lean sits about six points toward Republicans, and with no general-election polls or expert ratings yet available, the forecast rests on those fundamentals. That places Iowa in Lean Republican territory, though the uncertainty band is wide this far from Election Day.\n\nThe visible campaign activity so far is primary politics: Republicans will keep the first-in-the-nation Iowa caucuses, giving their candidates an early organizing presence in the state, while Democrats have again left Iowa out of their early calendar. That asymmetry may modestly help Republican groundwork, but its effect on the general election remains unclear. Early polling and the eventual nominees will do much to define the race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2447, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.291, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2906, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2896, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2832, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2898, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2916, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2874, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2897, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2848, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2852, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2903, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2933, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2792,